## Environment setup

Update `.env` values before running in non-local environments.

- Database type: `{{ db_config }}`
{% if db_config == "sqlite" %}
- SQLite path is configured via `DATABASE_PATH`
{% else %}
- Server DB uses `DATABASE_HOST`, `DATABASE_PORT`, `DATABASE_USER`, `DATABASE_PASSWORD`, `DATABASE_NAME`
{% endif %}
{% if with_auth %}
- Auth settings are controlled via `AUTH_ENABLED` and `JWT_*` variables
- **Roles:** seeding creates `SuperAdmin` and `User`. Open `register` assigns the **`User`** role by name. If the `User` role is removed, self-service registration returns **409** until it exists again (invites to other roles still work).
- **Single SuperAdmin:** at most one user may have the `SuperAdmin` role. The `SuperAdmin` role cannot be deleted via API; SuperAdmin users cannot be deleted via API. Bootstrap runs when no SuperAdmin exists yet. Empty `ADMIN_PASSWORD` always produces a one-time generated password printed once (stdout; local/dev). Set `ADMIN_PASSWORD` for a fixed bootstrap secret. User admin APIs require a SuperAdmin JWT and cannot create a SuperAdmin via `POST /users`.
- **Initial SuperAdmin (optional):** when `ENABLE_SEED` is `TRUE`, the first SuperAdmin for `ADMIN_EMAIL` uses `ADMIN_PASSWORD` if set, otherwise a one-time generated password (stored hashed only). That user has `must_change_password` until they call `POST /api/v1/auth/change-password`.
- If you change the user schema after a DB already exists, delete the SQLite file (or migrate) so `create_all` can apply the new columns.
{% endif %}
{% if with_email %}
- SMTP settings are controlled via `EMAIL_ENABLED` and `SMTP_*` variables
{% endif %}

